WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.968
-Our first guest tonight is
a Grammy-nominated

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.938
country-music star
who is also a coach on

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.906
the hit show "The Voice,"
which airs

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.675
Monday and Tuesday nights
here on NBC.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.675
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:10.743
-Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.712
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:16.983
My team is full!

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.884
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes!

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:22.988
-[ Chanting ] Blake, Blake,
Blake, Blake, Blake, Blake!

00:00:22.988 --> 00:00:25.558
-Let's go!

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:26.593
-Whoo!

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.927
It doesn't work.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.095
It doesn't work anymore.

00:00:30.095 --> 00:00:32.598
-Alright, Kelly Clarkson, it's
just me and you, sis.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:35.335
-♪ Just you and I ♪

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.670
-You got quite the team there,
my old man.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:38.738
-Old man?

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.539
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:43.342
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Blake Shelton.

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:44.611
How are you, Blake?

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.013
-[ Laughs ] I'm doing good.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.348
It's funny.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:51.350
I haven't seen that part of
the show aired back yet,

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:55.521
and it's a lot of fun to see
a universal superstar

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:58.624
like Ariana Grande
call me an old man...

00:00:58.624 --> 00:00:59.759
-Yeah.
-...on national television.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.861
That's great for
my ego and confidence.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.964
-Well, you've actually had
some ego issues over the years.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.498
This isn't the first time
that Ariana Grande

00:01:06.498 --> 00:01:07.933
has bumped up against your ego.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:10.536
There was a time where
you guys put out albums

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:11.804
on the same weekend.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:15.207
-[ Laughs ] I know.
Hey, I reminded her of that.

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:20.680
It was like -- That was in 2016,
and -- I don't know --

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.516
one of her huge albums came out,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.285
and I had a project
I was putting out called

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.319
"If I'm Honest."

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.487
And we were so excited about it.

00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:31.357
And I remember, the week
the album came out, I was like,

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.525
"What do you think
it's gonna --"

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.159
You know, you always
call your record label

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:35.695
and you're like, "What do you
think we're going to do?"

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.130
You know, you think it's going
to be number 1?"

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.399
And they're like,
"Well, you know, Ariana Grande's

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:41.634
album comes out this week.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.235
But you could get
number 2, maybe."

00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:46.906
So she took a dump on
those dreams, too.

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.174
By the way, great monologue.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:51.143
I was sitting here with
my brother-in-law,

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:54.213
sitting off-screen,
and you were mentioning about

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.615
getting a sunburn
on your taint.

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:59.586
And then -- And it started
a whole conversation about

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.321
"What's the difference
in a chode and a taint?"

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:03.489
And we've been --

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.558
And it's really --
It's a great show, man,

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.427
because it causes
these conversations.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:09.696
These conversations, you know?

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.398
-Yeah, we like to get people
talking about stuff

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:13.833
that they wouldn't
otherwise talk about.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:14.934
-Yeah.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.003
-You know, a brother-in-law,
of course,

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:20.005
is one of the many beneficiaries
of getting married,

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:21.540
and I want to
say congratulations,

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.209
because since
the last time we talked,

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:26.646
you officially
tied the knot with Gwen.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:30.049
-We did, man.
We did it back in July.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:34.186
And Gwen and I -- we agree that
if we're going to pull off

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:37.589
the ultimate publicity stunt,
which is what

00:02:37.589 --> 00:02:40.559
this relationship is,

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:42.462
then we wanted to
follow through, man.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.930
and go ahead and get married,
because, you know,

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.799
the next season of "The Voice"
was coming up,

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:50.536
and, you know,
we're team players for NBC.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:53.072
Which I am -- By the way,
I am your boss now.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.441
-You are my boss, deservedly so.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.876
I want to just say, like,
this is a photo --

00:02:57.876 --> 00:03:01.047
She is a beautiful bride.
You are also in this picture.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.449
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.784
-You know what
I love about that picture?

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:07.120
Is that her arm is perfectly
placed to drop --

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.789
to block my
double chin right there.

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:11.791
-That's true love right there.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.827
-You can't see the pelican chin
hanging down as much.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:18.064
-You were married by
Carson Daly.

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:20.833
Did you think, 20 years ago,
the host of "TRL"

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:24.369
would be the guy
helping you tie the knot?

00:03:24.369 --> 00:03:26.872
-Man, I tell you what.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:30.075
The way he handled those
wet-T-shirt contests

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:31.811
back in the day when
he was hosting those

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:34.480
spring-break specials,
we knew --

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.949
we knew he had to be
the guy for us.

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:38.518
-'Cause those things can get
pretty hairy.

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.586
If he can keep his cool there,
you know,

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:43.021
he is the right guy
for your big day.

00:03:43.021 --> 00:03:45.391
-He was -- I don't know
who was more excited.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.661
When we called Carson -- I mean,
we were a little bit nervous

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:51.430
to even ask him
because the guy's so --

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.699
I mean, he's so busy.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:54.233
I don't even know how he does --

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:56.035
Literally, he has a radio show.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:59.338
He has the "Today" show.
He has "The Voice."

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:02.141
And he used to have a show that
came on, you know,

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:04.910
after -- I guess, what,
two shows after your show.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.245
You know what I mean?

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:10.383
Like when nobody was watching.
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.951
Which is why
you probably didn't know

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.986
he doesn't have
that anymore, but --

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:15.120
-Now we just throw it to
the tumbleweeds.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.689
-And it was like, you know,
how are you

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.023
going to ask him
to do this thing?

00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:19.525
But he jumped on
the opportunity,

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.061
and he ended up staying there
with his family

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.829
for a few days with us.

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.631
It was awesome. It really was.

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:26.966
-So, this is interesting.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.535
So when I got married, you know,
we wrote our own vows.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:32.304
And I -- You know, being
somebody who writes comedy,

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:34.774
I found that pressure of, like,
wanting to be funny.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.875
You wrote a song
for your wedding.

00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:39.712
Did you feel the
same pressure to, actually,

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:42.348
do a song up to your standard?

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:44.416
-Well, I didn't feel pressure

00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:45.918
because she didn't know
I was going to do it.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.219
So I felt like, "You know,

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:51.290
there's really no bar,
you know, to set right here.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.992
But we agreed that
we were going to --

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:57.196
And it was Carson's idea
that we should write our own,

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.198
you know, vows or whatever.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:03.135
I have this piece to say
before we say "I do,"

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:08.207
and Gwen has always -- She is
constantly on my ass about

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.975
I should be writing more songs.

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:11.344
"How come you
don't write more songs?"

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:12.512
You know?

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:15.848
And I have gotten lazy
about it over the years.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:19.318
And so I decided,
"Well, you know, I'll step up

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:23.255
and come up with something,"
and so I did.

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:27.593
And we're putting it on --
I'm putting out a deluxe version

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.261
of this record that
we have out now,

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:31.797
and we're going to
put it on there.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:33.632
And so I'm excited.

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:35.334
I'm excited for people to
hear it, you know?

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.371
A lot of people ask me about it
since they found out

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:40.839
that I did that, and so I'm --
we're excited about it.

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:42.007
I want people to hear it.

00:05:42.007 --> 00:05:44.844
I mean, my God,
I married Gwen Stefani.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.413
I want all -- I want everybody
to hear that.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.649
I mean, that's
the ultimate bragging rights.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.450
-It's really good.
Did you -- I'm curious.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.885
When you were performing it
at the wedding,

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:54.721
was it an eye-contact situation?

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:57.156
Were you looking right at her
as you were doing the song?

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.457
-I did, I did.

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:02.395
I had rehearsed it
so many times just, you know,

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.897
in the bathroom or when we
weren't together or whatever

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:07.266
that I really had it down,
you know?

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:10.969
The only thing I was concerned
about was breaking the barstool

00:06:10.969 --> 00:06:12.838
that they had for me to sit on.

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:15.241
That was literally something
that was in my mind like,

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:18.510
"Oh, wouldn't that be great
if I sat on this thing, and..."

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.013
But I didn't. I made it through.
-I'm very glad to hear this.

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:23.182
This is -- You hit
a milestone, as well.

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.084
The 20-year anniversary of,
I guess,

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.887
your first big hit, "Austin."

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.655
-That's right.

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:32.325
-That was
the mulleted Blake Shelton,

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:35.060
who was not hanging with
Carson Daly back in the day.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.698
-Let me tell you something, man.
That mullet was underrated.

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:40.265
And I think it should come back.

00:06:40.265 --> 00:06:42.367
I don't know about -- Did you
ever have a mullet or --

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:44.670
Is this as long as your hair's
ever been, right now?

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.273
-This -- No, back in college,
it was very long.

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:49.275
I could put it
in a ponytail in college.

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:51.610
-But no mullet.
-No mullet, no.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.212
-Yeah. Well,
you missed out, buddy.

00:06:54.212 --> 00:06:55.581
You missed out on
all the action.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.849
Let me tell you.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:07:00.252
-You're coming up on
500 episodes of "The Voice."

00:07:00.252 --> 00:07:01.954
This is the 21st season.

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:04.390
It's been about 10 years now.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.792
And you get audiences
back after some time away.

00:07:06.792 --> 00:07:08.460
It just must be great to have
live audiences back

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.296
for a show like that.

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:15.500
-We had them for the
blind auditions this season,

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:17.570
and that's the first time in --

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.473
I guess, we went two seasons
without an audience,

00:07:20.473 --> 00:07:24.310
which was --
You know, it wasn't fun.

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.211
It's not the same, you know?

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:29.381
It's mostly for the people
who are auditioning,

00:07:29.381 --> 00:07:31.884
because, for us coaches,

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:34.253
it's not about
the audience, you know?

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:37.256
In fact, sometimes, it's
a distraction for us coaches.

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:40.159
But it's not as fun for,
I don't think,

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:43.562
the contestants not to have that
immediate feedback, you know?

00:07:43.562 --> 00:07:47.633
Especially if somebody doesn't
make it on to the show,

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.435
you know, at least
they get the sendoff like,

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:50.870
"You know, it will be okay."

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:54.206
You know, but nothing's worse
than when you didn't make it

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:56.408
and you have to have
that silent, you know,

00:07:56.408 --> 00:07:57.542
walk off the stage.

00:07:57.542 --> 00:07:59.678
It was just -- It's horrifying.

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:01.614
And so having the audience
back this season --

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.448
it just feels so much better.

00:08:03.448 --> 00:08:04.583
It's music, you know?

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:06.919
And so you want people
to be there.

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:09.855
-And, as the winningest coach,
how confident do you feel --

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:11.089
-Oh, you're talking about me.

00:08:11.089 --> 00:08:12.858
Oh, you're talking about me
when you say that.

00:08:12.858 --> 00:08:14.092
Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:14.092 --> 00:08:16.862
-How confident are
you right now, Blake?

00:08:16.862 --> 00:08:20.232
-Well, you know --
Listen, Ariana is a --

00:08:20.232 --> 00:08:24.703
She's a super-talented,
very sweet human being.

00:08:24.703 --> 00:08:27.874
I -- My feeling is,
she's going to suck as a coach.

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:28.941
-Yeah.

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:32.444
-And Kelly Clarkson --
I think her --

00:08:32.444 --> 00:08:34.246
it's kind of
fizzled out, you know?

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:36.282
Just too -- There's too much
Kelly on TV.

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:39.151
I joke that NBC
is "Nothing But Clarkson."

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:40.585
People are tired of her.

00:08:40.585 --> 00:08:41.821
People are sick
and tired of her.

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:43.122
-Yeah.

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:45.857
-And with John Legend, he's just
so high all the time,

00:08:45.857 --> 00:08:48.895
I don't even know if he knows
he's on TV, you know?

00:08:48.895 --> 00:08:52.030
And so I feel like this year's
going to be a gimme for me,

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.699
and I'm excited about it.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:55.167
-Well, it's always great
to have you here.

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:57.169
I would love -- If you could
do some research on

00:08:57.169 --> 00:08:59.071
the difference between
taint and chode,

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:00.438
and we'll talk about it
next time you're on.

00:09:00.438 --> 00:09:02.975
-I will. We'll do that.
He's Googling it right now.

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:05.911
We're looking at pictures.
We can tell by the pictures.

00:09:05.911 --> 00:09:07.947
-Hey, all the best, Blake.
It's always great to see you.

00:09:07.947 --> 00:09:09.848
-Thank you, buddy.

00:09:09.848 --> 00:09:12.351
-"The Voice" airs Monday
and Tuesday nights here on NBC.

